  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Diakonia Zambia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened Accountability Program II: Diakonia Zambia - Diakonia Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Diakonia arbetar i Zambia med att st&#xe4;rka medborgares f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else f&#xf6;r deras roll i, och hur de kan bidra till, den politiska, ekonomiska och sociala utvecklingen i landet. Diakonia arbetar ocks&#xe5; f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;ka f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;elsen f&#xf6;r vikten av j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och j&#xe4;mlikhet, samt att &#xf6;ka kvinnors deltagande i beslutsfattande.   

Under de senaste &#xe5;ren har Diakonia implementerat SAP-I programmet (finansierat av Sida), vars syfte har varit att se till att medborgare f&#xe5;r &#xf6;kad tillg&#xe5;ng till resurser. Diakonia f&#xf6;resl&#xe5;r nu att implementera en andra fas av projektet; SAP-II. Det nya programmet kommer att bygga p&#xe5; l&#xe4;rdomar av vad som fungerade/fungerade mindre bra under SAP-I, och en uppdaterad kontextanalys av Zambia. Diakonia ans&#xf6;ker om finansiering fr&#xe5;n Sida till ett v&#xe4;rde av SEK 41 400 000 f&#xf6;r perioden 2018&#x2013;2021, f&#xf6;r att implementera SAP-II. Ambassaden har allokerat SEK 1 000 000 f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra en oberoende utv&#xe4;rdering vid programmets slut (2021). 

SAP-II kommer att t&#xe4;cka ett st&#xf6;rre geografiskt omr&#xe5;de &#xe4;n SAP-I. Programmet kommer ocks&#xe5; att dubbla antalet samarbetspartner (fr&#xe5;n fem tio). Syftet &#xe4;r fortsatt att bidra till att medborgare f&#xf6;r &#xf6;kade m&#xf6;jligheter att p&#xe5;verka beslutsfattande, kr&#xe4;va transparens och ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande, och bidra till en mer r&#xe4;ttvis naturresursallokering. Diakonias l&#xe5;ngsiktiga m&#xe5;l med programmet &#xe4;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra livskvalit&#xe9;n f&#xf6;r samh&#xe4;llen (framf&#xf6;rallt f&#xf6;r kvinnor, ungdomar, fattiga och mest utsatta) i naturresursrika omr&#xe5;den i Zambia.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Diakonia is an international development organization made of two Swedish churches. The head office is located in Sweden. In Zambia, Diakonia works to increase Rights Holders (RHs) understanding of their role in political, social and economic development processes, the importance of achieving gender equality and increasing women&#x2019;s participation. 

Over the past years, Diakonia has been implementing their SAP-I programme (supported by the Embassy of Sweden) aimed to ensure that Right Holders (RHs) have increased access to resources through engagement with corporate and public sectors. Diakonia now proposes to implement  the SAP-Phase II (SAP-II) based on the achievements, lessons learned, best practices from the SAP-I and the current context in Zambia. Hence, Diakonia has applied to Sida for funding of SEK 41,400,000 for the period 2018-2021 to implement the SAP-II. The Embassy has also allocated a SEK1,000,000.00 for an independent end of program evaluation to be undertaken in 2021.

The SAP-II will see the expansion of the programme to new geographical areas while also scaling up coverage in additional sites in the previous targeted districts. The programme will continue to address challenges of vulnerable communities in predominantly rural areas by strengthening RHs participation in enhancing equality, transparency and accountability in national resource allocation. Diakonia&#xb4;s overall goal and expected long-term change with the SAP-II is to improve quality of life of communities (especially, women, youth, the poor and most vulnerable groups) in natural resource rich, rural and peri-urban areas of Zambia. The overall programme objective is to empower RHs to hold duty bearers accountable for equitable access and distribution of national resources.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Diakonia&apos;s overall goal and expected long-term change/impact with the SAP-II is to improve quality of life of communities (specifically women, youth, the poor and most vulnerable groups) in natural resource rich, rural and peri-urban areas of Zambia. This will be achieved through the empowerment of Rights Holders (men, women, youth) to hold duty bearers accountable for equitable access to and distribution of national resources.&#xa0;This will be implemented through ten (10) civil society organisations.
The SAP-II is also expected to lead to the following outcomes;
Program Outcome 1: Right holders (RHs), in targeted districts of Zambia are empowered to hold duty bearers accountable for equitable access and distribution of national resources (including natural resources);
Program Outcome 2: Targeted duty bearers (state institutions and corporates) are transparent and are accountable to right holders in the administration and governance of national/natural resources;
Program Outcome 3: Partner organisations have increased capacity to implement their mandates and effectively deliver rights based social, political and economic programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
